ng. And that's your old Ngu-ra-kul history, your language history, your sermon history, your skin name ceremony, your jurisdiction."}, {"start": "00:25:17", "end": "00:25:54", "text": "To exist in the homeland of the kangaroo, you have to understand. To understand it, we'll try and teach you to soar really high like the West Ham. It's like reading a book. The behavior of animals, the behavior of the change of character in them."}, {"start": "00:26:04", "end": "00:27:30", "text": "It's just a law from this country. It shapes us who we are. They call this crown land. I sometimes wonder what crown asks you to find out the original crown of this country in doing that you are like a military fulfilling your duty of care we call it grand result goes you fulfill something your fulfillment of carrying your country giving back to your country and that's it's all the knowledge for your own well-being from this country to give it back to people. In doing so, you already got the original crown, the emus crown."}, {"start": "00:27:41", "end": "00:29:21", "text": "The original crown is a Southern Cross here, because it's sitting on the emu's head. Yeah. To us, that's a whole ngurakulu. It's a reminder that we mustn't be like a little star drifting away. That's why the little stars is the homeland or this continent. and to learn all Darwan will expand your learning how you should live in this country. And firstly, you must learn all these archives in the whole Ngurakulu, the law, the skin name, the land, the ceremony, and the language. To live in the woman and the kangaroo, you have to understand the immune."}, {"start": "00:29:33", "end": "00:30:25", "text": "Your country will know you. I am a man. I am a man. I am a man."}, {"start": "04:42:50", "end": "04:43:29", "text": "Five o'clock in the morning is, yeah, maybe four sometimes. Yeah, you see, sunlight doesn't expand like we've always been drawing the sun coming up the mountains. Now, it shoots up, straight up, to us, that's gone all. During this year in ceremony, when the men sings, women dance, flicking their finger like that. So they get to expand the light going this way horizontally."}, {"start": "04:43:57", "end": "04:44:44", "text": "First, he has to grow like a tree, straight up. That means, yeah, everything is born unto you. Everything around you, yeah, gonna be you. Embrace them while you can. Learn about them. Because they'll guide you how you should live. Because you're gonna have to adapt to this house country. and enjoy its richness, I guess, with that knowledge. Because if you don't, your birch ride is stripped from you and your life falls short. It's a really hard country out here."}, {"start": "04:46:26", "end": "04:47:11", "text": "I'm learning through to these knowledges through the initiation ceremony of this place here. That's what I mean by negative and positive consequences of the law. It makes or breaks you. Haka and Albert, it's just the way the country is built or created, that's all."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:00"}, "track": {"title": "The Happening", "artists": [{"name": "Tomorrow Comes The Harvest"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:22:36"}, "track": {"title": "NGURRA KURLU (HOME)", "artists": [{"name": "Crown and Country"}, {"name": "Jerry Jangala Patrick"}, {"name": "MWNCI & Wanta Jampijinpa Pawu-Kurlpurlurnu"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:31:00"}, "track": {"title": "Show Me Love", "artists": [{"name": "Robin S."}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:32:00"}, "track": {"title": "I Want C & B to Fix My Car", "artists": [{"name": "Boof"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:34:00"}, "track": {"title": "Sound Check One", "artists": [{"name": "Pacho & Pepo"}]}, "isPremiere":